{"archetypes":[{"name":"caller-audit","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Plan names only two adopters of --require-result-pattern; other callers of dispatch-with-waterfall.sh that also run post-dispatch structure greps may be silently missed, and the out-of-scope exclusions exist only in the issue body","prompt_body":"Grep the repository for every invocation of dispatch-with-waterfall.sh and compare against the two callers the plan names (decompose-aggregator.sh, decompose-panel-dispatch.sh). For each unlisted caller, check whether it performs a post-dispatch structure grep on the output file; if so, flag it as a missing adoption site or confirm the plan's explicit out-of-scope rationale covers it. Also verify the out-of-scope exclusions (sketch-phase callers, plan-review collectors) are recorded in the modified .md files and not only in the issue body text. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-fidelity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Plan asserts 'capture argv into log already in place' for test-decompose-aggregator.sh, but if that log-capture path does not exist the two new assertions cannot pass; plan also claims env-driven stub extensions are purely additive","prompt_body":"Read skills/design/scripts/test-decompose-aggregator.sh and confirm whether the happy-path block already writes waterfall argv to a log file (wf.log or equivalent) before the plan adds the two new grep assertions against it. If no such capture exists, the plan's proposed assertions are broken as written. Similarly, read the cursor-stub and codex-stub sections in scripts/test-dispatch-with-waterfall.sh and verify that their current result-content generation is compatible with the plan's env-var extension (CURSOR_STUB_RESULT_CONTENT, CODEX_STUB_RESULT_CONTENT) so the new variables are genuinely additive and will not silently alter the byte-identical assertions the plan promises to preserve. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-scope","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Plan places a `continue` statement inside collect_phase to push pattern-mismatched slots into failed[], but `continue` is only valid inside a loop body; the plan must be verified against the actual function structure","prompt_body":"Read the collect_phase function (or equivalent per-slot processing block) in scripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh and confirm whether the insertion point the plan describes — after STATUS/REVIEWER_FILE extraction, using `continue` to skip into failed[] — is inside a for/while loop construct. If collect_phase processes a single slot and is invoked from an outer loop, a bare `continue` inside the function is a no-op or a syntax error depending on Bash version. Also verify that the plan's `failed+=(\"$idx\")` array-append syntax matches the existing array-mutation idiom already used elsewhere in the script, confirming no Bash 4-only constructs (declare -A, nameref, mapfile) are silently introduced in violation of the repo's Bash 3.2 portability requirement. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
